  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 306 AM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nSurface high pressure continues to expand across the region \nearly this morning in the wake of yesterday's cold front. This\nwill lead to a period of largely quiescent weather through the \nend of the week. A lake breeze is expected to push inland today \nwhich may provide enough lift for a few spotty showers or \nsprinkles as a weak disturbance moves across the area (15% \nchance). Coverage should remain very isolated if they even\ndevelop given limited moisture availability and shallow cloud \ndepths. Otherwise rain-free weather is in store across the area\nthrough at least Saturday afternoon with highs in the upper 70s\nto lower 80s and comfortable humidity.\n\nMostly clear skies early this morning and again tonight may \nallow for sufficient radiational cooling for shallow patchy fog \ndevelopment, particularly along river valleys and typical fog \nprone low spots outside of Chicago.\n\nLooking ahead, the upper level pattern begins to transition \ntoward upper ridging building across the central CONUS with \nmultiple waves expected to traverse the Northern Plains and \nUpper Midwest this weekend through much of the upcoming week. \nThe first of these waves may arrive as early as Saturday \nnight in the form of a decaying convective complex. Latest \nguidance suggests that if this convection forms upstream it \nwould likely be outrunning the unstable airmass with southeast\nextent and residual low-level dry air across the area would \nlikely limit the coverage of lightning or any potential severe \nweather here locally.\n\nThe degree of heating as well as our shower and thunderstorm \nchances for much of the upcoming week will be dependent upon the\nstrength of the aforementioned upper ridge. A stronger ridge \nwould result in warmer (potentially highs in the 90s) and more \nhumid conditions with the focus for greater thunderstorm \ncoverage ending up north of the area. In contrast, a weaker \nupper ridge would support warmer conditions but to a lesser \ndegree (mid-upper 80s) paired with frequent rounds of showers \nand thunderstorms. Suspect we may end up somewhere in between \nthese two scenarios and will continue to refine the details as \nit gets closer. Stay tuned.\n\nPetr",
